GoodPart Extender

> Keep the part that hits. Lose the rest.

GoodPart Extender is a local-first browser app for taking the strongest section of a song and turning it into a longer, seamless cut.

It is designed for music you own or have permission to transform.

What it does

• Loads audio locally in the browser
• Draws a waveform
• Lets the user mark a start and end point
• Repeats the selected section to a chosen duration
• Hides loop boundaries with crossfades
• Adds optional micro-variation so the result feels less mechanical
• Exports the result as a WAV file
• Uploads nothing to a server

Run it

1. Copy the code below into a file named index.html.
2. Open that file in a modern desktop browser.
3. Choose an MP3, WAV, M4A, or AAC file.
4. Mark the strongest section.
5. Set the length, crossfade, and variation.
6. Generate and export the result.

