Architecture

The current prototype uses the Web Audio API as an offline render engine:

```text
Audio file
    ↓
Decode to AudioBuffer
    ↓
Select high-value region
    ↓
Segment extraction
    ↓
Overlap + crossfade + controlled drift
    ↓
Peak normalization
    ↓
WAV encoding
```

Product direction

The current version is an intelligent extender rather than a fully generative music model. A production version could add:

• Beat and downbeat detection
• Bar-aligned selection snapping
• Key and chord estimation
• Stem separation
• Phrase-boundary detection
• Transition ranking
• Energy-curve controls
• Drum, bass, vocal, and harmony locks
• A licensed generative continuation backend
• Provenance and rights metadata

The deeper product primitive is not “loop this clip.” It is:

> Identify the musical attractor inside a recording, preserve its defining invariants, and generate additional time that remains inside that attractor.

